  "target_summary": "Hi [FREELANCER_NAME_001],\n\nApologies for being out of touch for several days; I have been focused on development in preparation for launch. I would now like to return to the website, since it will obviously be an integral component. The areas I want us to review and plan are:\n\n1\\. completing the assets and layout for the original landing-page design, including responsive behavior\n\n2\\. establishing the foundation for additional website pages—for example, whether they will share headers and footers, remain in \"dark mode,\" or use a complementary \"light mode\" treatment (not a switchable one)\n\n3\\. determining what general guidance and/or rules we can establish for responsive behavior\n\n4\\. designing the layout and visual styling for the dashboard shell and \"canvas\"\n\nFYI, I attached screens from the secure signup and login process that uses AWS Cognito. They currently rely on the AWS default appearance, although many self-styling options are available.\n\nSome of these items belong within the existing job, while others are beyond its scope. What approach would you recommend? Should we arrange an in-person meeting or a video call to go over them?\n\n[FREELANCER_NAME_002]",
